cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qGridX: qubit-efficient transmission planning with correlation-encoded optimization"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Boussahi
    given-names: Achraf
    email: achraftv2004@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Constantine Quantum Technologies, University Constantine 1 Freres Mentouri"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashrafboussahi/qGridX"
abstract: >-
  qGridX solves transmission planning problems on a handful of qubits. Each
  binary decision is stored in the sign of one multi-qubit Pauli correlation, so
  an n-qubit register carries 3*C(n,k) decisions and the device runs exactly
  three circuits at any problem size. A decoder-only transformer writes the
  circuit and is trained only on the cost of fully decoded, budget-feasible
  plans, so no gradient crosses into the quantum device. The package includes
  storage siting and microgrid formation models built from DC optimal power
  flow, an N-1 security screen, and the device execution path used to measure
  the encoding on a 108-qubit superconducting processor.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - combinatorial optimization
  - Pauli correlation encoding
  - generative quantum eigensolver
  - power systems
  - transmission planning
  - N-1 security
